## goat-cli profile (ADR 1019)

{% if goat_cli_bundle_minted | default(false) %}
Your cert tarball (downloaded + unpacked above) **already contains** a
signed **CBOR profile bundle**, `{{ manifest.zenoh.trial.vendor }}-goat-cli.cbor`,
that loads everything (cert, key, CA roots, portal token, endpoint pair)
into `~/.goat/contexts/default/` in one command. No separate file to
fetch — it rides the same tarball as your cert.

The offline-CA signature covers the whole tuple (cert + key + token +
endpoints + ca-roots), so an attacker who tampers with the tarball in
transit can't swap the portal endpoint while keeping a valid cert.

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| CBOR bundle | `{{ manifest.zenoh.trial.vendor }}-goat-cli.cbor` (in your cert tarball) |
| Mode | `0400` (sensitive — contains your private key + portal token) |
| Bundle CA | `{{ goat_cli_ca_id_map.get(zenoh_trial_site, 'dev-' ~ zenoh_trial_site ~ '-ca') }}` |

**Install the `goat` binary** (macOS / Linux only — run after NetBird is
up, the download host is mesh-only):

```bash
OS=$(uname -s | tr 'A-Z' 'a-z')                      # darwin | linux
ARCH=$(uname -m | sed 's/x86_64/amd64/;s/aarch64/arm64/')
DL=$(mktemp -d)                                      # private download dir, not a shared /tmp name
curl -fsSL {{ goat_get_base_url | default('https://get.' ~ zenoh_trial_site ~ '.netbird.' ~ zenoh_trial_site ~ '.net') }}/goat-${OS}-${ARCH} -o "$DL/goat"
[ "$OS" = darwin ] && codesign --force --sign - "$DL/goat"   # macOS: clear the launch hang, before the move
sudo mkdir -p /usr/local/bin
sudo install -m 0755 "$DL/goat" /usr/local/bin/goat
goat --version                                       # /usr/local/bin is on PATH everywhere
```

No Windows build — on Windows, skip the CLI and use the web surfaces
(portal / panoscope / brief) in a browser.

**Then load your profile (one-time), from the unpacked tarball dir:**

```bash
goat ca add {{ manifest.zenoh.trial.vendor }}-goat-cli-ca.pem      # trust the CA that signed your bundle, once per goatnet
goat profile init {{ manifest.zenoh.trial.vendor }}-goat-cli.cbor
```

`goat` ships trusting no goatnet, so `profile init` refuses (`E_BUNDLE_INVALID`
— wrong CA) until the root that signed your bundle has been added — run
`goat ca add` first. The `-goat-cli-ca.pem` sits beside the `.cbor` in the
tarball. `goat ca add` prints a SHA-256 fingerprint: check it against one
your operator gave you out of band before you rely on it. `goat ca ls`
shows what you already trust.

`goat profile init` then verifies the CA signature against the root you
just added, writes the cert + key + CA-roots + portal token + profile.toml
into `~/.goat/contexts/default/` (dir `0700`, files `0600`), then
runs `goat doctor` to verify reachability across all four steps
(ZTOL membership, Zenoh router TCP+TLS, mTLS session, portal
`/api/vendors`).

Then:

```bash
goat profile show       # confirm endpoints + cert expiry
goat doctor             # re-run any time to validate reachability
```

For topic CRUD, pub/sub, stethoscope delegation, vendor browse —
see `goat --help` or the goat-cli design doc inside the repo.

